From d828d052f4efa2b952309a12a693f76bdace49fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:03:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 826/826] feat(responses): support CustomTool and OpenResponses
 input normalization

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-61-r2's series applied through 0825.

Rationale: Codex CLI and OpenResponses clients send Responses API requests with
{"type": "custom", "name": "apply_patch"} tools, custom_tool_call /
custom_tool_call_output history items across context compaction, and typeless or
id-less assistant/reasoning input items (#1206). Port the non-Harmony Responses
API custom-tool shim (upstream vllm-project/vllm@83773ecdf3ce) and OpenResponses
input normalization (upstream vllm-project/vllm@945d0a268bc6) so free-form text
custom tools are schema-shimmed as single-string {"input": ...} functions for
chat templates, decoded back into custom_tool_call output items and
response.custom_tool_call_input.{delta,done} SSE events, and reconstructed cleanly
on multi-turn history replay (including empty ResponseOutputMessage content and
dict-form reasoning/assistant inputs). Grammar-formatted custom tools are
explicitly rejected with a 400 validation error.

Quality implications: Responses API frontend and tool schema helpers only; no
impact on chat completions, inference kernels, CUDA graphs, memory layout, or
serving benchmarks.

Tests: CPU pytest tests/entrypoints/openai/test_responses_custom_tools.py in
the candidate-61-r2 container covering CustomTool validation, Codex apply_patch
compaction history replay, custom tool streaming deltas/done events, schema and
xgrammar helpers, and OpenResponses input normalization.

Upstream status: adapted from upstream vllm-project/vllm commits 83773ecdf3ce
(#57322) and 945d0a268bc6 (#35508) for the 19f2c20ed4d6 non-Harmony stack.
